{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"**As of 6 November 2026**, distinguish three obligations:\n\n- **Transparency-policy disclosure:** Explain the portfolio-transparency policy and where portfolio information—and any indicative NAV—is available. Disclosure of a policy is **not itself a requirement to publish full holdings daily**.\n- **Daily public holdings:** Full daily portfolio publication is one transparency model, not an unconditional requirement for every Irish UCITS ETF or ETF share class.\n- **Conditional periodic route:** CBI Q&A 1012 (April 2025) permits periodic public holdings disclosure subject to conditions, including daily information enabling authorised participants/market makers to undertake effective arbitrage. That daily information need not mean daily **public** disclosure of the full portfolio.\n\nI cannot verify the bank draft or its identified 2026 regulations here, so cannot confirm the precise publication timetable, conditions or statutory cross-references.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Policy disclosure, public holdings publication and professional arbitrage information are distinct requirements; none should be treated as interchangeable."}}
